\name{PerformanceMeasures}
\alias{PerformanceMeasures}
\title{Return, risk and benchmark-relative measures calculated from closing prices}
\description{
The last link of the chain of analysis classes, which \code{Instrument} and \code{AssetBasket} inherit, so the same Sharpe ratio or drawdown can be asked of one share, an index, a fund or a whole basket.

Each public method fetches candles through \code{prices()}, works on the closing prices, and returns one number, or a \code{data.frame} for \code{drawdowns()}, or a named list for \code{performance_summary()}.

Returns are the fractional change of the close from one candle to the next. Annual figures scale by the number of candles in a trading year, 252 for \code{day} candles and the number of candles in 252 sessions of 375 minutes for an intraday interval such as \verb{5minute}. A \code{risk_free_rate} is an annual fraction, so 6.5 percent is 0.065.
}
\examples{
